      "As for when it is connected to the alif of duality, examples are: \"The two friends travel tomorrow\" and \"You two travel tomorrow.\" The words \"they travel\" and \"you travel\" are mudāriʿ verbs in the state of rafʿ due to them being free from particles of naṣb or jazm. The sign of them being marfūʿ is the presence of the letter nūn and the alif is the subject. From this it can be seen that the mudāriʿ verb connected to this letter alif will sometimes commence with the letter yā to indicate the third person, and sometimes commence with the letter tā to indicate the second person.",
